#import "template.typ": *

#let metadata = (
  title: "RPC Cross Country/Navigation Endorsement Flight Test",
  unit: "Cross Country Endorsement | Flight Test",
  author: "C.Moroney",
  version: "v1.0.0",
)

#let lesson = (
title: [#metadata.title]

,aim: [
Demonstrate all elements, to the required standard, for the issue of the RAAus Cross Country endorsement.
]

,overview: [
The cross country endorsement flight test is conducted by the CFI or DCFI, and will assess the candidates ability to perform all elements in the RAAus Cross Country syllabus to an RPC standard. That is, ensuring that the candidate, without assistance and within tolerances, can: navigate an aircraft using DR and pilotage to a foreign airfield at least 75nm away while avoiding CTR and SUA; conduct a circuit join and landing at the foreign airfield; navigate low level and perform diversions. The examiner will expect the candidate to perform all navigation tasks without the aid of an EFB.

This lesson plan is a reference document for both the examiner and the student. It does not contain new instruction — it documents the structure and requirements of the formal test.
]

,learning_outcomes: [
All elements at C standard — as defined in each element's lesson plan and in the RAAus syllabus of flight training flight tolerance table.
]

,theory_knowledge: [
All theory exams confirmed passed before the test date. No new theory for this lesson.
]

,ground_brief_topics: [
Total time: 30 minutes \
Equipment required: Student logbook, training record, all exam results, POH, NAIPS access, student's pre-planned flight plan, navigation equipment, PLB, flight test paperwork \

*Final Pre-Test Administrative Gate* (15 minutes)

All of the following must be sighted and confirmed by the examiner before the flight test proceeds:

_Logbook:_
- ☐ Pilot logbook complete and up to date; all flights entered; all columns completed; all signatures present
- ☐ Total cross country aeronautical experience: minimum 14 hours
- ☐ Solo cross country PIC time: minimum 2 hours
- ☐ CFI endorsement in logbook confirming the student has met all training requirements and is recommended for flight test

_Theory exams — results sighted:_
- ☐ Navigation and Meteorology: passed (minimum 80%, KDR completed)

_RAAus membership and currency:_
- ☐ Valid RAAus Pilot Certificate
- ☐ Valid BFR
- ☐ Financial flying membership current
- ☐ Health declaration current

_Training record:_
- ☐ All cross country elements recorded at C standard
- ☐ Solo navigation completed and graded at C standard

*Test Brief* (30 minutes)
- Examiner confirms the flight test format: examiner role; no coaching; candidate plans and conducts the complete flight
- Candidate briefs the planned flight: flight plan, weather, NOTAMs, fuel requirements, diversion plans
- Examiner will ask oral theory questions during the ground brief
]

,ground_tasks:[
#text(size:12pt)[*Candidate*]
- Uses appropriate charts, as well as NAIPS TAF/GAF/GPWT, ERSA and other relevant documents to create a valid flight plan; checks BOM radar; briefs conditions and suitability
- Ensures all required equipment (including emergency equipment) is carried and serviceable.
- Reviews maintenance release; briefs examiner on all items checked

#text(size:12pt)[*Examiner*]
- Sights and confirms all administrative gate items before proceeding
- Receives candidate's full brief; will ask oral questions to assess depth of knowledge
- Does not provide any flight planning assistance, apart from telling the candidate the desired route; assesses the brief as presented
- Proceeds only when all gate items are confirmed
- Provides a briefing of the conditions of the test (see in flight tasks below)
]

,in_flight_tasks:[
#text(size:12pt)[*Flight Test — Candidate as PIC, Examiner as Assessor*]
The examiner does not coach, prompt, or intervene except for safety. All assessment is silent.\

If the examiner must take control of the aircraft at any point, the test will be considered unsuccessful.\

The examiner will take over for the following reasons:
- The candidate fails to maintain adequate aircraft control
- The candidate fails to notice a deviation in aircraft attitude, such that an unusual attitude or other undesirable aircraft state is imminent
- The candidate fails to maintain separation with CTA or SUA, such that a breach is imminent (the examiner will not take control or prompt before such time)
- The candidate fails to maintain adequate separation from another aircraft

The flight test covers all navigation elements, connected as sequence. The examiner may request specific emergency elements during the flight. At minimum the following must be demonstrated:

- Standard navigation: DR and pilotage used to effect a pre-planned route; arrival at the DR target within 5nm and ±3 minutes; at least 1 demonstration of an effective 1-in-60 correction; frequencies managed and monitored effectively; fuel managed and recorded correctly; flight log maintained.
- Diversions: Diversion to an unplanned airfield or ground feature; arrival at the diversion target within 5nm and ±5 minutes; CLEAROFF completed, frequencies and (if applicable) airfield arrival procedures conducted correctly; fuel managed and recorded correctly; flight log maintained.
- Low Level: Conduct a low level diversion to an airfield or ground feature, using the correct technique (slow aircraft, follow ground feature); maintain the tolerance set by the examiner (ie. cloud is at 1200 feet AGL); correctly identify the diversion target; maintain terrain separation an separation from other aircraft at all times.
- Arrival/Departure procedures: Complete a circuit join, landing and departure at a foreign airfield effectively and correctly, accounting for any traffic and airfield conditions

#text(size:12pt)[*Examiner*]
- Records C or NC for each element
- Intervenes only for the reasons stated above
- If a safety issue requires intervention — notes it; assesses whether the candidate's actions would have resolved the situation independently
- Automatic NC for any control intervention
]

,common_errors:[
Not applicable — this is a formal assessment, not an instructional lesson.
]

,post_flight:[
- *Examiner Debrief* (20 min):
  - Reports C or NC for each element with specific evidence
  - If all elements at C standard: recommends candidate for RPC Cross Country Endorsement; completes RAAus flight test paperwork; signs logbook
  - If one or more elements NC: explains what was observed; does not recommend; candidate must remediate and rebook with CFI
  - Provides verbal acknowledgement of the candidate's demonstrated strengths

- *If recommended:*
  - Examiner completes and signs RAAus Endorsement Recognition form
  - Candidate's logbook endorsed with RAAus Endorsement
  - CFI notified and training file closed

- *If not recommended:*
  - NC elements clearly recorded with evidence
  - Remediation plan agreed with candidate and CFI
  - Flight test may be rebooked with CFI after targeted remediation
]

,standards_for_progression:[
*Flight test pass requirements — all must be met:*

_Administrative gate (confirmed before test proceeds):_
- ☐ Logbook complete; minimum 14 hours total cross country; minimum 2 hours solo cross country PIC
- ☐ CFI/DCFI endorsement for flight test in logbook
- ☐ Navigation and Meteorology exam passed
- ☐ All elements at C standard in training record

_In-flight assessment:_
- All elements demonstrated to C standard per the RAAus syllabus of flight training/FIRM flight tolerance table
- Flight planned and conducted independently; no coaching from examiner

*Endorsement is issued when all administrative and in-flight requirements are met.*

- *Outcome*: Test result recorded on RAAus form and in student training record. Endorsement is issued or remediation plan agreed.
]

,safety:[
- *Weather*: All element-specific minima apply; examiner confirms conditions are suitable before the test proceeds; if conditions deteriorate during the test — examiner may terminate and reschedule
- *Examiner authority*: The examiner has full authority to terminate the flight test at any time for safety reasons; a termination for safety does not automatically result in a fail — the examiner assesses whether the safety issue was caused by the candidate or by external factors
- *TEM*:
  - Flight test anxiety is normal; the examiner should establish a calm, professional tone during the ground brief
  - If the candidate appears significantly distressed before the flight — the examiner may defer the test; a distressed candidate is unlikely to demonstrate their true capability
  - All emergency simulations (EFATO, FLWOP) are clearly briefed before the flight; the examiner confirms the candidate's understanding before initiating any simulation
]

,homework:[
No homework — this is the final assessment. After the flight test:
- If recommended: register with RAAus; obtain RPC; review the conditions and limitations of the certificate
- If not recommended: review the specific NC items; schedule remediation with the CFI; approach the retest with a clear understanding of what specifically needs to be different
]
)

#show: body => lesson_plan(metadata, lesson, body)